  recipeId: robotics
  concept: 'Authored objective: Repair three independent axis faults.

    Authored
    requirement: Diagnose and repair axis C drive, encoder D via and axis F thermal
    feedback. Requalify after each repair.

    General teaching principle: Motion
    validation must consider correct reference, feedback, interlocks and authored
    limits before declaring a movement safe or accurate.

    Only fresh, authoritative
    game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A coordinated team needs agreement on position and timing before everyone
    moves.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Motion feedback and a command signal are not interchangeable evidence
    of successful positioning.
  baseline: "Before working on \u2018Repair three independent axis faults\u2019,
    which component, reference or condition mentioned in the authored requirement
    should you inspect first? Explain your reasoning."
  prediction: "For \u2018Repair three independent axis faults\u2019, what result
    or observation would you expect if the required setup is correct? Distinguish
    a predicted result from a measured result."
  practice: "In Level 120, perform the objective \u2018Repair three independent axis
    faults\u2019 in the actual game laboratory. Compare fresh evidence against: Diagnose
    and repair axis C drive, encoder D via and axis F thermal feedback. Requalify
    after each repair.\nThe mission evaluator decides completion; this tutorial does
    not grade your answer."
